---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import '../../../styles/detail.css';

const title = 'Steel Structure Workshop | Industrial Factory Building | ZhongSai';
const description = 'ZhongSai Steel Structure provides steel structure workshop solutions for industrial manufacturing projects, covering design detailing, fabrication, component supply, packing and export delivery, with support for crane requirements and equipment layout planning.';
const lang = 'en';
const canonical = 'https://zhongsai-steelstructure.com/en/steel-workshop/';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="detail-hero">
    <div class="detail-hero-bg" style="background-image: url('/images/products/app-industrial-workshop-hero.jpg');"></div>
    <div class="detail-hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="detail-hero-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Industrial Workshop · Factory Building</span>
      <h1>Steel Structure Workshop for Industrial Manufacturing Projects</h1>
      <p class="lead">ZhongSai Steel Structure delivers steel structure workshop solutions for manufacturing projects. From design detailing to fabrication and export, we support equipment layout, crane requirements and production space planning to turn your facility needs into deliverable steel structure buildings.</p>
      <div class="detail-hero-actions">
        <a href="#quote" class="btn btn-primary">Get Project Quotation</a>
        <a href="/en/products/" class="btn btn-outline">View All Products</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <nav class="detail-breadcrumb">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/en/">Home</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <a href="/en/products/">Products</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <span class="current">Industrial Workshop</span>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- 01 Workshop Project Requirements -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">01 / Project Requirements</p>
        <h2>What Information Is Needed for a Steel Structure Workshop</h2>
        <p>The structural configuration of an industrial workshop depends on production use, equipment layout and operating environment. At the proposal stage, the following information directly influences column grid, building height, crane and enclosure system design.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="requirement-grid">
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="req-icon">01</div>
          <h3>Building Use</h3>
          <p>Production manufacturing, processing and assembly, equipment workshop or mixed use — different processes require different space and load configurations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="req-icon">02</div>
          <h3>Equipment Layout</h3>
          <p>Dimensions, weight, location and operating space of main production equipment affect column grid layout and structural load design.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="req-icon">03</div>
          <h3>Working Space</h3>
          <p>Required clear working height, aisle width, material storage areas and space reserved for future expansion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="req-icon">04</div>
          <h3>Crane Requirement</h3>
          <p>Whether overhead cranes are needed, crane capacity, operating range and rail top height should be confirmed during structural design.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="req-icon">05</div>
          <h3>Ventilation & Lighting</h3>
          <p>Production process requirements for ventilation, smoke exhaust and natural lighting influence roof openings and enclosure system configuration.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="req-icon">06</div>
          <h3>Enclosure Requirements</h3>
          <p>Roof and wall materials, thermal insulation, waterproofing grade and other enclosure needs are determined by operating environment and project requirements.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 Structural & Production Space Planning -->
  <section class="detail-section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">02 / Structural & Space Planning</p>
        <h2>Structural and Production Space Planning Around Workflow</h2>
        <p>The core of an industrial workshop is production efficiency. Structural planning needs to accommodate equipment layout, production flow and material handling, rather than simply pursuing maximum span.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="image-text-block">
        <div class="itb-image">
          <img src="/images/company/factory-interior-production.jpg" alt="ZhongSai steel structure workshop production space" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="itb-content">
          <h3>Column Grid Coordinated with Production Space</h3>
          <p>Column grid spacing is determined based on equipment dimensions, production aisles and material handling routes, balancing structural economy with usable production space.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Column grid spacing coordinated with equipment layout and production flow</li>
            <li>Clear working height accommodates equipment operation and access</li>
            <li>Crane requirements confirmed and reserved during structural design</li>
            <li>Roof and wall systems coordinated with structural frame</li>
            <li>Specific spans, heights and loads determined per project drawings and requirements</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03 Steel Structure Fabrication -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">03 / Steel Fabrication</p>
        <h2>From Drawings to Fabricated Steel Components</h2>
        <p>ZhongSai Steel Structure operates its own production base, covering cutting, assembly, welding, straightening, drilling, surface treatment and quality control. Steel components are fabricated according to project drawings.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-card reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="feature-img" style="background-image: url('/images/company/factory-steel-beam-fabrication.jpg');"></div>
          <div class="feature-body">
            <h3>Steel Beams & Columns</h3>
            <p>H-beams, box sections and other primary structural members are cut, assembled and welded per shop drawings, with dimensional accuracy controlled per project requirements.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="feature-img" style="background-image: url('/images/manufacturing/real/workshop-overview-wide-9815.jpg');"></div>
          <div class="feature-body">
            <h3>Fabrication & Quality Control</h3>
            <p>Fabrication is organized per project drawings and technical specifications, with dimensional, welding and visual inspection at key stages. Specific inspection requirements follow project agreements.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top: 28px; display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a href="/en/manufacturing-quality/" class="btn btn-outline">View Manufacturing Capability</a>
        <a href="/en/components/fabricated-steel-beams-columns/" class="btn btn-outline">Steel Beams & Columns</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 Roof & Wall Systems -->
  <section class="detail-section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">04 / Roof & Wall Systems</p>
        <h2>Roof and Wall Cladding Systems</h2>
        <p>The enclosure system of an industrial workshop directly affects operating environment and operational cost. ZhongSai can supply roof panels, wall panels and supporting cladding materials per project requirements, coordinated with the primary steel structure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="image-text-block reverse">
        <div class="itb-image">
          <img src="/images/products/detail-cladding-system.jpg" alt="Steel structure roof and wall cladding systems" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="itb-content">
          <h3>Cladding Configuration Determined Per Project</h3>
          <p>Roof and wall materials, thermal insulation, waterproofing grade and ventilation configuration are determined based on building use, local climate and project technical requirements.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Roof and wall panel systems can be supplied together with the primary structure</li>
            <li>Thermal insulation layers configured per operating environment and project requirements</li>
            <li>Roof drainage and waterproofing details designed per project technical requirements</li>
            <li>Ventilation and lighting openings coordinated with the cladding system</li>
          </ul>
          <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <a href="/en/components/roof-wall-cladding-systems/" class="btn btn-outline">View Cladding Systems</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 From Drawings to Export Supply -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">05 / Drawings to Export</p>
        <h2>Complete Process from Project Drawings to Export Delivery</h2>
        <p>ZhongSai provides steel structure supply services from design detailing to export delivery. Local construction is performed by the customer or local construction team.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-flow">
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="step-num">01</div>
          <h4>Drawings Confirmation</h4>
          <p>Project drawings, BOQ and technical requirements confirmed</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="step-num">02</div>
          <h4>Design Detailing</h4>
          <p>Detailing design and fabrication drawing preparation</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="step-num">03</div>
          <h4>Fabrication</h4>
          <p>Steel component fabrication organized per drawings</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-4">
          <div class="step-num">04</div>
          <h4>Component Marking</h4>
          <p>Component marking and numbering may be arranged based on shop drawings</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="step-num">05</div>
          <h4>Packing & Loading</h4>
          <p>Packing organized by component type and container loading requirements</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="step-num">06</div>
          <h4>Export Documentation</h4>
          <p>Export documentation support and logistics coordination</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="step-num">07</div>
          <h4>Sea Freight Delivery</h4>
          <p>Container loading and sea freight export arrangement</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-4">
          <div class="step-num">08</div>
          <h4>Technical Guidance</h4>
          <p>Overseas installation technical guidance (local erection by customer team)</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GEO Service Boundary -->
  <section class="detail-section dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center;">Service Boundary</p>
        <h2 style="color: #fff;">What ZhongSai Provides and Does Not Provide</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto;">Clear service scope to avoid project expectation gaps.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="geo-boundary">
        <div class="geo-box include">
          <h4>ZhongSai Provides</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Design detailing and fabrication drawing support</li>
            <li>Steel component fabrication</li>
            <li>Steel beams, columns, trusses and component supply</li>
            <li>Roof and wall cladding system coordination</li>
            <li>Component marking, packing and container loading</li>
            <li>Export documentation support and logistics coordination</li>
            <li>Overseas installation technical guidance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="geo-box exclude">
          <h4>ZhongSai Does Not Directly Undertake</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Local construction in the project country</li>
            <li>Local foundation construction</li>
            <li>Local general contracting / EPC</li>
            <li>Local finishing and MEP works</li>
            <li>Customs brokerage as a licensed customs broker</li>
            <li>Freight forwarding as a licensed freight forwarder</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 06 What We Need for Quotation -->
  <section class="detail-section alt" id="quote-info">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">06 / Quotation Information</p>
        <h2>What Information Is Needed for a Workshop Quotation</h2>
        <p>The more complete the project information, the more accurate the quotation. Length, width and height alone cannot provide an accurate quotation — use, equipment and technical requirements must be considered.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="quote-info-grid">
        <div class="quote-info-card drawing">
          <h4>Have Drawings / BOQ</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Project country</li>
            <li>Architectural / structural drawings</li>
            <li>Bill of Quantities (BOQ)</li>
            <li>Project technical specifications</li>
            <li>Crane / equipment special requirements</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="quote-info-card no-drawing">
          <h4>No Complete Drawings Yet</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Project country</li>
            <li>Building use (production / processing / equipment)</li>
            <li>Length / width / height (reference dimensions)</li>
            <li>Crane requirement (capacity / quantity)</li>
            <li>Main equipment layout description</li>
            <li>Other special requirements</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="quote-note">* Initial proposal and quotation require needs assessment based on project use and basic parameters. Final proposal and pricing are subject to drawing and technical requirement confirmation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 07 FAQ -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center;">07 / FAQ</p>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Steel Workshops</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="detail-faq">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can I start without complete drawings?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Yes. You can first provide project use, basic dimensions, equipment layout and crane requirements. ZhongSai can conduct initial needs assessment and confirm what is needed for proposal and quotation. However, accurate pricing requires complete drawings and technical specifications.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>What information is needed if the workshop requires a crane?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              You need to provide crane capacity, quantity, operating range, rail top height and duty cycle. Crane requirements directly influence structural design and should be confirmed at the proposal stage — adding cranes later is not recommended.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can ZhongSai supply only fabricated steel components?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Yes. ZhongSai can supply steel beams, columns, trusses and other steel components separately based on project drawings, or together with roof and wall cladding systems. The supply scope is determined per project requirements.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 08 Quote CTA + QuoteForm -->
  <section class="detail-section dark" id="quote">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center; color: #f59e0b;">08 / Get Quotation</p>
        <h2 style="color: #fff;">Submit Your Industrial Workshop Project Requirements</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);">Upload drawings if available, or submit basic project requirements if you don't have complete drawings yet.</p>
      </div>
      <QuoteForm lang="en" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // FAQ toggle
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-question').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const item = btn.closest('.faq-item');
      const isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');
      item.classList.toggle('open');
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !isOpen);
    });
  });

  // Scroll reveal
  const revealElements = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach(entry => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.style.opacity = '1';
          entry.target.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';
          observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.1 });
    revealElements.forEach(el => {
      el.style.opacity = '0';
      el.style.transform = 'translateY(24px)';
      el.style.transition = 'opacity 0.6s ease, transform 0.6s ease';
      observer.observe(el);
    });
  }
</script>
